Subject: [PATCH 2/5] docs(cdd/issue): add mode declaration + MCA preconditions

Adds an explicit mode-declaration section to cdd/issue/SKILL.md
naming four modes (MCA / explore / design-and-build / docs-only)
and three preconditions for MCA:

  1. Design committed at a stable path (not issue body)
  2. Plan committed with explicit step ordering
  3. Both stable for the duration of the cycle

When mode = MCA, the issue's source-of-truth table must cite both
the design and the plan paths. Without these rows the mode is
mis-labeled.

Adds two checklist items: mode declaration and MCA citation.

Motivation: the cnos-tsc supercycle produced empirical evidence
that mis-labeled MCA cycles inflate review pressure. Cycles with
stable design+plan ran in 1-2 rounds; cycles where alpha had to
re-derive the plan ran in 3 rounds. The skill spec previously
mentioned MCA but did not name preconditions, leaving room for
gamma to assert MCA without the upfront artifacts that make MCA
work.
